From afa6617faa6aca48da00e9e25ff5f46911d2f0ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rob Vogelaar <rob.vogelaar@libertyglobal.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 19:30:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] cli: stabilize layout and show client channel

Settle topology optimization synchronously so its final fit does not look like
a delayed two-second polling redraw. Keep the colocated controller and Agent
close while giving wireless extender links more room.

Publish each client's authoritative radio band and operating channel through
the clients and topology APIs. Show band and channel in the client table and
topology, and include channel and serving BSSID in client hover details.

After the Agent's first successful topology synchronization, reconcile its
cached current operating classes with OneWifi's live per-radio RBUS channels
and send one unsolicited standard Operating Channel Report per radio. This
closes the startup subscription race and seeds the Controller even when no
Channel Selection Request was needed during onboarding.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [HWSIM evaluation WebUI]
